   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="poem">
            <pb n='1'/>
            
               <lg>
                  <l>In the young spring evening</l>
               <l>The moon is shining full</l>
               <l>Girls form a circle</l>
               <l>As though round an altar</l>
               </lg>
               <lg>
                  <l>And their feet perform</l>
               <l>Rhythmical steps</l>
               <l>Like the soft feet of Cretan girls</l>
               <l>Must once have danced</l>
               </lg>
               <lg>
                  <l>Round and round an altar of love</l>
               <l>Designing a circle</l>
               <l>In the delicate flowering grass</l>
               </lg>
               <lg>
                  <l>The stars that are shining</l>
               <l>Around the beautiful moon</l>
               <l>Hide their own bright faces</l>
               </lg>
               <lg>
                  <l>When She, at Her fullest</l>
               <l>Paints the earth with Her</l>
               <l>Silvery light</l>
               </lg>
               <lg>
                  <l>Now, while we are dancing</l>
               <l>Come! Join us!</l>
               <l>Sweet joy, revelry,</l>
               <l>Bright light!</l>
               </lg>
               <lg>
                  <l>Inspire us, Muses</l>
               <l>Oh, you with the beautiful hair.</l>
               </lg>
               <byline>—Sappho</byline>
           
            <note>translated from the Greek by Charoula</note>
         </div>
